PASS -- both stated scope limits are closed.  The tail holds across
the Brillouin zone, so the phase convention is right and not merely
right at the one symmetric point; and its error behaves as an
expansion that the near-shell radius controls.

⚠ This does NOT by itself make the route a safe default: the cost
is still 3.55x, and the mixed-contrast channel's convergence ORDER
remains unverified because its error passes through zero.
